{%- comment -%}
  Rosey: the tagged <div> is this component's root, so the block's _uuid is
  folded into the key instead of being emitted as data-rosey-ns on the same
  element (the build and the editor would resolve different keys otherwise).

  `roseyKey` is an optional, template-only param. Parents that render several
  textBlocks as sub-fields (heading: eyebrow / headline / description) pass a
  distinct key per include together with `_uuid: ""`, so the blocks neither all
  key as `text` nor inherit the parent's _uuid a second time:

    {% bookshop "generic/textBlock" text: content.headline _uuid: "" roseyKey: "headline" %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture textBlockKey -%}{{ _uuid }}:{{ roseyKey | default: "text" }}{%- endcapture -%}
{% if text and env_bookshop_live %}
    <div  class="c-textBlock w-full"{{ text | roseyMarkdown: textBlockKey }}>
        {{ text | markdownify  }}
    </div>
{% elsif text %}
<div class="c-textBlock w-full"{{ text | roseyMarkdown: textBlockKey }}>
        {{ text | renderContent | markdownify  }}
    </div>
{% endif %}